        "transcript": "What about Carlos?"
    },
    {
        "id": 90,
        "start": 432.48,
        "end": 436.16,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00232.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Can you find another adverb in the sentence?"
    },
    {
        "id": 91,
        "start": 436.16,
        "end": 438.96,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00233.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Even if they were not complete."
    },
    {
        "id": 92,
        "start": 438.96,
        "end": 441.52,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00234.png",
            "frame_00235.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "You still have this one."
    },
    {
        "id": 93,
        "start": 441.52,
        "end": 447.44,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00236.png",
            "frame_00237.png",
            "frame_00238.png",
            "frame_00239.png",
            "frame_00240.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "It's presenting a condition."
    },
    {
        "id": 94,
        "start": 447.44,
        "end": 454.64,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00241.png",
            "frame_00242.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "So you have three kinds of adverbs in this sentence."
    },
    {
        "id": 95,
        "start": 454.64,
        "end": 459.6,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00243.png",
            "frame_00244.png",
            "frame_00245.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "The first one is a single word adverb, which is well."
    },
    {
        "id": 96,
        "start": 459.6,
        "end": 463.92,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00246.png",
            "frame_00247.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "This adverb modifies perform."
    },
    {
        "id": 97,
        "start": 463.92,
        "end": 468.64,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00248.png",
            "frame_00249.png",
            "frame_00250.png",
            "frame_00251.png",
            "frame_00252.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "And performed is a verb."
    },
    {
        "id": 98,
        "start": 468.64,
        "end": 473.12,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00253.png",
            "frame_00254.png",
            "frame_00255.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "The second one that's encircled is the word not."
    },
    {
        "id": 99,
        "start": 473.12,
        "end": 476.16,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00256.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "And the word not here describes what word?"
    },
    {
        "id": 100,
        "start": 476.16,
        "end": 477.76,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00257.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Janbundak."
    },
    {
        "id": 101,
        "start": 477.76,
        "end": 485.0,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00258.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "[Silent] for 7.52 sec"
    },
    {
        "id": 102,
        "start": 485.0,
        "end": 486.4,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00259.png",
            "frame_00260.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Are you sure?"
    },
    {
        "id": 103,
        "start": 486.4,
        "end": 490.96,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00261.png",
            "frame_00262.png",
            "frame_00263.png",
            "frame_00264.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "It's an adverb, therefore it should not describe a pronoun."
    },
    {
        "id": 104,
        "start": 490.96,
        "end": 495.6,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00265.png",
            "frame_00266.png",
            "frame_00267.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "What is the verb?"
    },
    {
        "id": 105,
        "start": 495.6,
        "end": 502.08,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00268.png",
            "frame_00269.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Adverbs do not only describe verbs, you also have adjectives or other adverbs."
    },
    {
        "id": 106,
        "start": 502.08,
        "end": 505.68,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00270.png",
            "frame_00271.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "What's described by not?"
    },
    {
        "id": 107,
        "start": 505.68,
        "end": 508.48,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00272.png",
            "frame_00273.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "What's modified by not in the sentence?"
    },
    {
        "id": 108,
        "start": 508.48,
        "end": 509.44,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00274.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Were."
    },
    {
        "id": 109,
        "start": 509.44,
        "end": 512.4,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00275.png",
            "frame_00276.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Lorraine, what about you, Lorraine?"
    },
    {
        "id": 110,
        "start": 512.4,
        "end": 513.12,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00277.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Is it were?"
    },
    {
        "id": 111,
        "start": 513.12,
        "end": 518.16,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00278.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Complete."
    },
    {
        "id": 112,
        "start": 518.16,
        "end": 520.32,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00279.png",
            "frame_00280.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "It's the word complete, correct."
    },
    {
        "id": 113,
        "start": 520.32,
        "end": 524.96,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00281.png",
            "frame_00282.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "To what part of speech does the word complete belong, Lorraine?"
    },
    {
        "id": 114,
        "start": 524.96,
        "end": 529.92,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00283.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Adjective."
    },
    {
        "id": 115,
        "start": 529.92,
        "end": 531.68,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00284.png",
            "frame_00285.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "It's an adjective."
    },
    {
        "id": 116,
        "start": 531.68,
        "end": 537.36,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00286.png",
            "frame_00287.png",
            "frame_00288.png",
            "frame_00289.png",
            "frame_00290.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Again, as defined, adverbs may modify verbs."
    },
    {
        "id": 117,
        "start": 537.36,
        "end": 540.4,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00291.png",
            "frame_00292.png",
            "frame_00293.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "They may also modify adjectives."
    },
    {
        "id": 118,
        "start": 540.4,
        "end": 542.56,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00294.png",
            "frame_00295.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "What about this clause?"
    },
    {
        "id": 119,
        "start": 542.56,
        "end": 546.64,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00296.png",
            "frame_00297.png",
            "frame_00298.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Even if they were not complete, what is it trying to modify?"
    },
    {
        "id": 120,
        "start": 546.64,
        "end": 548.96,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00299.png",
            "frame_00300.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Juliana?"
    },
    {
        "id": 121,
        "start": 548.96,
        "end": 557.0,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00301.png",
            "frame_00302.png",
            "frame_00303.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "[Silent] for 8.32 sec"
    },
    {
        "id": 122,
        "start": 557.0,
        "end": 559.2,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00304.png",
            "frame_00305.png",
            "frame_00306.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Performed, correct."
    },
    {
        "id": 123,
        "start": 559.2,
        "end": 563.76,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00307.png",
            "frame_00308.png",
            "frame_00309.png",
            "frame_00310.png",
            "frame_00311.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "So this goes back to performed, which is a verb."
    },
    {
        "id": 124,
        "start": 563.76,
        "end": 568.56,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00312.png",
            "frame_00313.png",
            "frame_00314.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Making this an adverb as well."
    },
    {
        "id": 125,
        "start": 568.56,
        "end": 572.56,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00315.png",
            "frame_00316.png",
            "frame_00317.png",
            "frame_00318.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Because performed is a verb."
    },
    {
        "id": 126,
        "start": 572.56,
        "end": 578.8,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00319.png",
            "frame_00320.png",
            "frame_00321.png",
            "frame_00322.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "So earlier, the question is, what are the adverbs in the sentence?"
    },
    {
        "id": 127,
        "start": 578.8,
        "end": 584.8,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00323.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "The answers given by Teya are the single word adverbs."
    },
    {
        "id": 128,
        "start": 584.8,
        "end": 591.28,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00324.png",
            "frame_00325.png",
            "frame_00326.png",
            "frame_00327.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "But there's one more, and that's this clause, adverb, this adverbial clause."
    },
    {
        "id": 129,
        "start": 591.28,
        "end": 601.2,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00328.png",
            "frame_00329.png",
            "frame_00330.png",
            "frame_00331.png",
            "frame_00332.png",
            "frame_00333.png",
            "frame_00334.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "And take note, the adverbial clause begins with a subordinating conjunction."
    },
    {
        "id": 130,
        "start": 601.2,
        "end": 609.12,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00335.png",
            "frame_00336.png",
            "frame_00337.png",
            "frame_00338.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "It's not right if you simply identify it from they until complete."
    },
    {
        "id": 131,
        "start": 609.12,
        "end": 612.96,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00339.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "We cannot do that because the clause is a dependent clause."
    },
    {
        "id": 132,
        "start": 612.96,
        "end": 618.48,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00340.png",
            "frame_00341.png",
            "frame_00342.png",
            "frame_00343.png",
            "frame_00344.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "And as a rule, dependent clauses begin with subordinating conjunctions."
    },
    {
        "id": 133,
        "start": 618.48,
        "end": 628.08,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00345.png",
            "frame_00346.png",
            "frame_00347.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "And if you look at your module, you'll have there the different occasions, locations in a sentence where you could put a dependent clause as an adverb."
    },
    {
        "id": 134,
        "start": 628.08,
        "end": 631.76,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00348.png",
            "frame_00349.png",
            "frame_00350.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Now let us check the activities in your modules."
    },
    {
        "id": 135,
        "start": 631.76,
        "end": 644.0,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00351.png",
            "frame_00352.png",
            "frame_00353.png",
            "frame_00354.png",
            "frame_00355.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "[Silent] for 12.64 sec"
    },
    {
        "id": 136,
        "start": 644.0,
        "end": 645.76,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00356.png",
            "frame_00357.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "We begin with FT1."
    },
    {
        "id": 137,
        "start": 645.76,
        "end": 652.48,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00358.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "The goal in FT1 is to simply identify single word."
    },
    {
        "id": 138,
        "start": 652.48,
        "end": 655.84,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00359.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "They note single word adverbs."
    },
    {
        "id": 139,
        "start": 655.84,
        "end": 659.04,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00360.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "So no one should underline a phrase."
    },
    {
        "id": 140,
        "start": 659.04,
        "end": 666.32,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00361.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "If one number has more than one answer, let's just still give it one point."
    },
    {
        "id": 141,
        "start": 666.32,
        "end": 674.72,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00362.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "If there are two answers in that number, but you only identified only one, you won't get a score."
    },
    {
        "id": 142,
        "start": 674.72,
        "end": 684.8,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00363.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "It's a matter of whether you'll get everything right or you don't before you get a point in that number."
    },
    {
        "id": 143,
        "start": 684.8,
        "end": 692.72,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00364.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "For a while, there."
    }
]